{"note":"One-piece knob with a captive, hand-pressed M5 hex nut. The nut loads from the underside; a split snap lip retains it when inverted, and the smaller through-bore plus the solid far-side seat prevent it passing through the far side. The separate M5x30 screw is optional listed hardware for use with the knob. Print with the nut-entry face on the bed. PLA snap features can vary with printer calibration; press the nut in steadily and stop if the tabs show cracking.","params":{"knob_d":{"value":30,"unit":"mm","kind":"design","source":"design","note":"Outside diameter."},"knob_h":{"value":13,"unit":"mm","kind":"design","source":"design"},"nut_af":{"value":8,"unit":"mm","kind":"hardware","source":"catalog","note":"ISO 4032 M5 hex nut across flats."},"nut_h":{"value":4.7,"unit":"mm","kind":"hardware","source":"catalog","note":"ISO 4032 M5 nut height."},"pocket_clearance":{"value":0.25,"unit":"mm","kind":"design","source":"design","note":"Added to nut across-flats dimension for the main hex pocket."},"throat_reduction":{"value":0.7,"unit":"mm","kind":"design","source":"design","note":"Across-flats reduction at the retaining throat; the slotted lower wall flexes as the nut is pressed past it."},"ramp_h":{"value":0.9,"unit":"mm","kind":"design","source":"design"},"nut_recess":{"value":1.5,"unit":"mm","kind":"design","source":"design","note":"Recess below the nut's seated position."},"bore_d":{"value":5.6,"unit":"mm","kind":"design","source":"design","note":"Clearance bore for an M5 bolt; smaller than the nut's outside dimensions."},"slot_width":{"value":0.6,"unit":"mm","kind":"design","source":"design","note":"Six vertical relief slots around the snap wall."},"slot_start_r":{"value":3.7,"unit":"mm","kind":"design","source":"design"},"slot_end_r":{"value":11.4,"unit":"mm","kind":"design","source":"design"},"slot_height":{"value":3.5,"unit":"mm","kind":"design","source":"design"}},"parts":[{"id":"knob","role":"final","material":"PLA","code":"import math
import cadquery as cq

def hex_points(af):
    r = af / math.sqrt(3.0)
    return [(r * math.cos(math.radians(60*i)), r * math.sin(math.radians(60*i))) for i in range(6)]

def hex_prism(af, z, height):
    return cq.Workplane('XY').polyline(hex_points(af)).close().extrude(height).val().translate(cq.Vector(0, 0, z))

def hex_wire(af, z):
    w = cq.Workplane('XY').polyline(hex_points(af)).close().wire().val()
    return w.translate(cq.Vector(0, 0, z))

def build(p):
    depth = p.nut_h + p.nut_recess
    cavity_af = p.nut_af + p.pocket_clearance
    throat_af = p.nut_af - p.throat_reduction
    body = cq.Workplane('XY').circle(p.knob_d / 2.0).extrude(p.knob_h).val()
    lead = cq.Solid.makeLoft([hex_wire(throat_af, 0), hex_wire(cavity_af, p.ramp_h)], True)
    body = body.cut(lead)
    body = body.cut(hex_prism(cavity_af, p.ramp_h, depth - p.ramp_h))
    body = body.cut(cq.Solid.makeCylinder(p.bore_d / 2.0, p.knob_h, cq.Vector(0, 0, 0)))
    slot_len = p.slot_end_r - p.slot_start_r
    for i in range(6):
        slot = cq.Solid.makeBox(slot_len, p.slot_width, p.slot_height,
                                cq.Vector(p.slot_start_r, -p.slot_width/2.0, 0))
        slot = slot.rotate((0, 0, 0), (0, 0, 1), 60*i)
        body = body.cut(slot)
    return body","print_orientation":"Place the circular nut-entry face at z=0 on the build plate; the bolt bore is vertical.","use_orientation":"Nut-entry side faces down when the knob is held in normal use; the opposite face is the bolt-head side."}],"hardware":[{"id":"nut","ref":"ISO 4032 M5","qty":1},{"id":"bolt","ref":"ISO 4762 M5x30","qty":1}],"criteria":[{"id":"nut_seat","part":"knob","feature":"Internal hex pocket, sized for the M5 nut; nut seats against the closed far-side shoulder.","relation":"seats","hardware":"nut","clearance_mm":0.25,"params":["nut_af","nut_h","pocket_clearance"],"check":{"method":"measure","description":"Press the nut in from the entry face. Confirm it seats fully inside the knob and that the far-side shoulder prevents it passing through."}},{"id":"nut_retention","part":"knob","feature":"Split snap throat at the nut-entry face.","relation":"contains","hardware":"nut","params":["throat_reduction","slot_width","slot_height"],"check":{"method":"measure","description":"After pressing the nut past the lip, turn the knob upside down and confirm the nut stays captured without adhesive. Do not force it if the PLA tabs crack."}},{"id":"bolt_bore","part":"knob","feature":"Through-bore from the far face into the captive nut.","relation":"clears","hardware":"bolt","clearance_mm":0.3,"params":["bore_d"],"check":{"method":"measure","description":"Pass the M5 bolt through the bore and engage it with the nut; confirm the threaded end can emerge from the nut-entry side."}}],"manual":[{"n":"1","text":"Print the knob with the nut-entry face on the build plate. Let it cool fully before fitting the nut.","parts":["knob"]},{"n":"2","text":"Align the M5 nut with the hex pocket and press it in from the entry face, steadily, until it seats against the internal shoulder and snaps past the retaining lip. The nut remains recessed inside the knob.","parts":["knob"],"hardware":["nut"],"tool":null},{"n":"3","text":"Check retention by turning the knob upside down. The nut should stay captured without glue. If the fit is too tight or the snap tabs crack, stop rather than forcing it.","parts":["knob"],"hardware":["nut"]},{"n":"4","text":"Feed the M5x30 bolt from the opposite face through the clearance bore and thread it into the captive nut. Its threaded end can emerge from the nut-entry side.","parts":["knob"],"hardware":["bolt","nut"]}]}
